Text:
This design is about how the user of fearlessManager binds Presses to the values that a Fearless program receives.
An 'input family' of a code project is a concrete type of that project implementing base.PressReleaseInput; the 'values' of an input family are the types that its .enumList lists.
In this design, TypeName names an input family, and TypeName' names one of its values.
Info, Infos.msg, Infos.list, Infos.map, TypeName, ProjectName, Base16, Target, Project and the Defines of fearlessManager are the ones of the designs of fearlessManager.
The Project of the designs of fearlessManager maps one more key, #inputs, to an Inputs; a Project that is registered starts with #inputs mapped to Infos.map().
The Message of the designs of fearlessManager has the forms of InputMessage too, and the Error of those designs has the forms of InputError too.
A Press that is a key of an Infos.map stands for its .str, as a TypeName does: Press.str is a bijection from the values of Press to some values of Str.
The bindings are per project: two projects with the same input family have independent Bindings.
When a Run starts, fearlessManager gives each main of that Run the Inputs of the Project of that Run.
A value with no Press in the FamilyBindings of its input family is never received by the program.
The manager GUI shows, for a code project, each input family of the project with its values, and the Presses bound to each value.
//later: the manifest of a package lists the input families of the package and their values
//later: an input family suggests default Presses for its values
//later: the keys that a text widget uses to edit and to move the caret are set here too, per project

Grammar:
Bindings ::= (Press1->TypeName1) .. (Pressn->TypeNamen)
FamilyBindings ::= Infos.map(Press1, Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Pressn, Infos.msg(TypeNamen))
Inputs ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, FamilyBindings1 .. TypeNamen, FamilyBindingsn)
InputMessage ::= "Bind " Target " " TypeName " " Press " " TypeName' \
               | "Unbind " Target " " TypeName " " Press
InputError ::= inputErrorPressCanNotBeBound(TypeName,Press)
#inputs in Str

Well formedness:
in Bindings: Press1.bindable .. Pressn.bindable
in Bindings: Bindings.strip(Press1) = Press1 .. Bindings.strip(Pressn) = Pressn
in FamilyBindings: FamilyBindings.bindings is of form Bindings

Notation: Infos.map(Press1, Infos.msg(TypeName1) .. Pressn, Infos.msg(TypeNamen)).bindings = (Press1->TypeName1) .. (Pressn->TypeNamen)

Notation: Bindings.keep("") = ""

Notation: Bindings.keep(Modifier "+") = "" where:
- (_Mods Modifier->_) in Bindings

Notation: Bindings.keep(Modifier "+") = Modifier "+" where:
- (_Mods Modifier->_) not in Bindings

Notation: Bindings.strip(ShiftMod CtrlMod AltMod SuperMod Key) = Bindings.keep(ShiftMod) Bindings.keep(CtrlMod) Bindings.keep(AltMod) Bindings.keep(SuperMod) Key

Notation: Press' in Bindings.blocked where:
- (Press->_) in Bindings
- Bindings.strip(Press') = Press
- Press' != Press
- not Press'.bindable

Notation: Inputs.family(TypeName) = FamilyBindings where:
- Inputs = Infos.map(_ TypeName, FamilyBindings _)

Notation: Inputs.family(TypeName) = Infos.map() where:
- Inputs is not of form Infos.map(_ TypeName, FamilyBindings _)

Text:
A Modifier that is the Key of a Press of Bindings is a 'bound modifier' of Bindings.
Bindings.strip(Press) removes the bound modifiers from the Mods of Press: with Shift bound to a value, W with Shift down is the Press W, so the two values are received together.
A Modifier that is not a bound modifier stays in the Mods: with A bound to a value and Alt bound to no value, A with Alt down is the Press Alt+A, and Alt+A is not the Press A.
The second WellFormednessLine of Bindings refuses a Press whose Mods holds a bound modifier: no Key going down would ever give that Press.
Bindings.blocked is the set of the 'blocked' Presses: a blocked Press is made only of Keys that are bound one by one, and still no program receives it.
For example, with Ctrl, Alt and T bound to three values, Ctrl+Alt+T is blocked: a desk opens a terminal for it.
A Press is about the Key that goes down last: with T down first, Ctrl and Alt going down after give the Presses Ctrl and Ctrl+Alt, which are not blocked.

Define fearlessManager$delegate("Bind Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ") " TypeName " " Press " " TypeName'):
A action fearlessManager$checkFullTargetIsCorrect("Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")")
B fact fearlessManager.projectsInfo.get(Base16) = Project
C fact Project.#inputs = Inputs
D fact Inputs.family(TypeName)[+=(Press->Infos.msg(TypeName'))] = Info
E if Info is not of form FamilyBindings, error inputErrorPressCanNotBeBound(TypeName,Press)
F action return "EditMetadata " fearlessManager.projectsInfo[Project=Project[#inputs=Inputs[+=(TypeName->Info)]]]

Define fearlessManager$delegate("Unbind Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ") " TypeName " " Press):
A action fearlessManager$checkFullTargetIsCorrect("Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")")
B fact fearlessManager.projectsInfo.get(Base16) = Project
C fact Project.#inputs = Inputs
D action return "EditMetadata " fearlessManager.projectsInfo[Project=Project[#inputs=Inputs[+=(TypeName->Inputs.family(TypeName)[/=Press])]]]

Text:
In the manager GUI, the user binds by pressing.
The user chooses a value TypeName' of an input family TypeName of a project, then presses keys or mouse buttons inside the 'manager window'.
The 'chosen Press' is the Press of the last Key that went down before the first Key goes up: Shift down, W down, any Key up gives Shift+W; Shift down, Shift up gives Shift.
In the three Stories below, Target names that project, FamilyBindings is the Inputs.family(TypeName) of that project, FamilyBindings' is FamilyBindings[+=(Press->Infos.msg(TypeName'))], and Message is "Bind " Target " " TypeName " " Press " " TypeName'.
When FamilyBindings' is not of form FamilyBindings, managerGui$send(Message) shows the InputError of the Answer, as for every other Message.
The 'disclaimer' is a dialog of the 'manager window' that lists Press1 .. Pressn, each with the values that its Keys are bound to, and has one tick box and one button to confirm.

Story:
A event The user chooses the Press Press for the value TypeName' of the input family TypeName.
B fact FamilyBindings' is not of form FamilyBindings, or every Press of FamilyBindings'.bindings.blocked is in FamilyBindings.bindings.blocked.
C action managerGui$send(Message)

Story:
A event The user chooses the Press Press for the value TypeName' of the input family TypeName.
B fact FamilyBindings' is of form FamilyBindings.
C fact Press1 .. Pressn are the Presses of FamilyBindings'.bindings.blocked that are not in FamilyBindings.bindings.blocked, and n is not 0.
D action The manager GUI shows the disclaimer for Press1 .. Pressn.
E event The user ticks the tick box and confirms.
F action managerGui$send(Message)

Story:
A event The user chooses the Press Press for the value TypeName' of the input family TypeName.
B fact FamilyBindings' is of form FamilyBindings.
C fact Press1 .. Pressn are the Presses of FamilyBindings'.bindings.blocked that are not in FamilyBindings.bindings.blocked, and n is not 0.
D action The manager GUI shows the disclaimer for Press1 .. Pressn.
E event The user closes the disclaimer without confirming.
F after The manager GUI has sent no Message.

Story:
A event The user removes the Press Press from the input family TypeName of the project that Target names.
B action managerGui$send("Unbind " Target " " TypeName " " Press)

Implementation notes:
A Str is a Fearless string literal: #inputs is "inputs", and Press.str is the Fearless string literal holding the text of Press.
Nothing stores which blocked Presses the user accepted: a Bind asks only for the blocked Presses that the Bind adds, and the Bindings that projects.info already holds were accepted when they were made.
On a desk that takes the chosen Press for itself, the 'manager window' never sees that Press, so the user can not choose it there; fearlessManager refuses the same Press on every desk through Press.bindable, and does not rely on what the 'manager window' sees.
The text of the disclaimer names the values first and the Keys after, for example: while Crouch and Walk are held, pressing Talk does nothing (Ctrl+Alt+T).
